From: DroidDeck-Mali, after emir34-34/DroidDeck 8f260546 + 3d6ede4b
Date: 2026-10-14
Subject: kbase on glibc: report the node's own device numbers as the DRM render and primary device

kbase exposes no DRM nodes, so the physical device was left with
drm.render_rdev and drm.primary_rdev at zero and VkPhysicalDeviceDrmPropertiesEXT
reported no device at all. Everything that matches a Vulkan device to a DRM node
by device number then simply never matches - gamescope's WSI among them, which is
what decides whether the session presents zero-copy or falls back to a copy.

In the Linux runtime that number is knowable: proot presents the kbase node itself
as the session's render node (tools/linuxfs/preload/drm.c picks /dev/mali0 and
synthesizes a DRM device for it), so this node's st_rdev *is* the render node's. It
is reported as the primary node too, because gamescope's nested Wayland backend
refuses a device with no primary node and the runtime has no KMS node to offer in
its place.

Guarded to non-Android builds: the bionic half puts frames on a real Android
surface and must keep whatever the platform reports.

Reference: emirvapur11, emir34-34/DroidDeck, commits 8f260546 ("Add experimental
MediaTek (Arm Mali) GPU support") and 3d6ede4b ("panvk: report the kbase node as
the DRM primary device too"), where it is patch 0001 of that fork's PanVK build.
Not upstream in wonderkast02/panvk-g720-kbase-csf g720-development ca16389.

--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
@@ -1285,7 +1285,23 @@ panvk_physical_device_init_kbase(struct panvk_physical_device *device,
    }
 
    /* kbase does not expose DRM nodes, so drm.{render,primary}_rdev are left
-    * zeroed; WSI paths that compare rdev values will simply not match. */
+    * zeroed; WSI paths that compare rdev values will simply not match.
+    *
+    * The glibc build is the exception: the Linux runtime presents the kbase
+    * node itself as the session's DRM render node, so this node's device
+    * number is the render node's, and reporting it is what lets gamescope
+    * match this device to the compositor's main device. It stands for the
+    * primary node too: gamescope's nested backend refuses a device without
+    * one and the runtime has no KMS node to offer in its place. */
+#ifndef __ANDROID__
+   {
+      struct stat st;
+      if (stat(path, &st) == 0 && S_ISCHR(st.st_mode)) {
+         device->drm.render_rdev = st.st_rdev;
+         device->drm.primary_rdev = st.st_rdev;
+      }
+   }
+#endif
 
    device->formats.all = pan_format_table(arch);
    device->formats.blendable = pan_blendable_format_table(arch);
